--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Monaco Editor (https://github.com/microsoft/monaco-editor)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The desktop app (apps/desktop) depends on the monaco-editor package for its
editor and diff viewer.

monaco-editor incorporates third-party components. Their notices are in the
ThirdPartyNotices.txt that ships in the package: the Node.js path library
(MIT), marked (MIT), TypeScript (Apache-2.0, with its own notices for
DefinitelyTyped (MIT), Unicode data (Unicode License), the W3C DOM (W3C
Software License), the WHATWG DOM (CC-BY-4.0), Web Background Synchronization
(W3C Community Final Specification Agreement) and WebGL (Khronos, MIT-style)),
the HTML 5.1 W3C Working Draft (W3C document licence), JS Beautifier (MIT),
Ionic documentation (Apache-2.0) and vscode-swift (MIT). It also bundles a
copy of DOMPurify (Apache-2.0 or MPL-2.0), which that file does not list; its
licence banner is kept at the top of esm/vs/base/browser/dompurify/dompurify.js
in the package.

